# Reserved. As of the current build, wiki-server does not read ANY
# environment variable — admin credentials live in the SQLite `users`
# table (set via `wiki-server --create-admin`), and sessions are random
# opaque tokens validated by a database lookup, not signed by a secret.
#
# This file exists as a documented hook for something that might
# genuinely need a runtime secret later (e.g. a Phase 2 remote MCP
# transport's bearer token) — the systemd unit references it via
# `EnvironmentFile=-/etc/wiki/wiki.env` (the leading '-' makes it
# optional, so its absence does not stop the service from starting).
#
# There is currently nothing to put in this file. If you find yourself
# wanting to add something here, first check whether wiki-server's config
# loader (src/config/AppConfig.cpp) actually reads it — if not, wiring
# that up is a prerequisite, not just dropping a KEY=value line here.
